  "Question": "In \\(\\triangle ABC,\\) \\(AB=BC=29,\\) and \\(AC=42.\\) What is the area of \\(\\triangle ABC?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( 100 \\)",
    "B": "\\( 420 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 500 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 609 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 701 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Since \\(AB=BC\\), the triangle is isosceles. Drawing the altitude from \\(B\\) to the base \\(AC\\) creates two right triangles and bisects the base, allowing us to find the height.\n\nLet \\(D\\) be the foot of this altitude. Then\n\\[\nAD=DC=\\frac{42}{2}=21.\n\\]\nIn right triangle \\(ABD\\), the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\\[\nBD^2=29^2-21^2=841-441=400.\n\\]\nBecause \\(BD\\) is a positive length, \\(BD=20\\). Therefore the area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is\n\\[\n\\frac12\\times42\\times20=420.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{420}\\) square units, choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
